"""Explicit B0007 section-level source decisions, not keyword classifiers."""
import json
import ledger as L
from review_batch_0001 import evidence
# suffix, filename, inspected pages, relevance, contribution, findings, remaining check
SPECS=[
('nn506014s','3617364-nn506014s_si_001.pdf','pp2–3','design_bearing','modified_design','Sameside sharp triangle preserves original scaffold arrangement/register but relocates staple nicks to one face. Amine variant replaces15 inner-edge staples with18T linkers and hybridizes a21A aminated strand; authors distinguish actual substoichiometric labeling from recommended protocol. ZIP inventory confirms named caDNAno JSON and staple XLS.','Inspect source members and exact15 replacements; do not substitute recommended concentrations for performed experiments.'),
('la503754e','3848170-la503754e_si_001.pdf','pp3–5,7–9','uncertain','uncertain','Supplement describes X-DNA hydrogel networks in lipid strata and four X1–X4 sequence species. It does not establish a scaffolded origami design in the inspected sections despite the title terminology.','Read primary synthesis/topology and inspect FigS1 image before deciding broad origami relevance; no title-based exclusion.'),
('nl5046473','3619440-nl5046473_si_001.pdf','pp2–3','design_bearing','modified_design','p8634 origami ring template is folded with variant elongated handles for nanoparticle attachment. Purified AuNP/AgNP assemblies and a four-attachment-site example are described.','Inspect Table1 handle combinations, template routing and complete parent/core sources; nanoparticle ring composition is not a separate core sequence set.'),
('nn505825z','3827749-nn505825z_si_001.pdf','pp2–3,9–11','design_bearing','modified_design','Explicit periodic connectivity maps define m13 and AT/CG-rich SQ2, HC2, SQ4 and SQ6 model plates; scaffold segments connect across simulation boundaries. SQ2/HC2 have32/21bp unit-cell helices.','Inspect main experimental versus computational scope and TableS2; retain periodic simulation models separately from finite physical origami and catalog eligibility.'),
('nl5045633','3821839-nl5045633_si_001.pdf','pp3–5,29–30','design_bearing','new_design','Bistable compliant four-bar mechanism is experimentally folded and TEM characterized. Closing/releasing strands actuate overhangs. FigS15 distinguishes main mechanism from fixed-joint stiffness-test design; TableS2 labels core and overhang staples.','Inspect both routing images and full TablesS2–S3, preserve distinct test construct and actuation states; source completeness unverified.'),
('ph500434f','3819664-ph500434f_si_001.pdf','pp2–3','design_bearing','modified_design','Rectangular M13mp18 origami carries four capture-strand sets for nanorod dimer arrangements. Assembly explicitly omits side staples100–111 and205–216. Baseline sequences follow schematic.','Map capture replacements for each configuration and reconcile listed baseline strands with explicit omissions; inspect routing.'),
('acs.nanolett.5b00351','3812992-nl5b00351_si_001.pdf','pp2–3','design_bearing','modified_design','Origami platform incorporates start/target extensions, asymmetry hairpins and tether anchor. Separate88bp tether, cargo, protection and removal strands are assembled in staged procedures.','Inspect section7 sequences and platform routing; distinguish mobile cargo/tether from core modifications and enumerate anchor variants.'),
('nn507035g','3798103-nn507035g_si_001.pdf','pp2–3','design_bearing','modified_design','18HB has protruding paired21mer ssDNA at42.9nm intervals. TEM captions identify Alexa488, IgG and ferritin functionalized variants following purification.','Acquire main assembly sources, parent design and exact functionalization strands; cargo variants need not imply distinct DNA cores.'),
('acs.jpclett.5b00747','3634551-jz5b00747_si_001.pdf','pp2–3','design_bearing','modified_design','Rectangular origami breadboard captures a tip-to-tip gold nanorod dimer. AFM and electrophoresis characterize core and hybridized structures; appendix is cited for capture strands.','Inspect appendix and primary assembly methods; resolve parent reference1, docking replacements and dye positions.'),
('acs.nanolett.5b01461','3623109-nl5b01461_si_001.pdf','pp2–3; primary XML Fig3 and assembly Methods','design_bearing','reused_design','Primary results experimentally fold a rectangle with an adaptable scaffold loop using7249/7560/8064nt scaffolds, plus pointer7249,42HB7560 and gear8064 designs. Source-production method includes actual design reuse.','Resolve parent sources and sequence/routing for each object; rectangle loop variants and multilayer designs must remain separate.'),
('acsnano.5b01841','3623535-nn5b01841_si_001.pdf','pp2–3,5–6','design_bearing','modified_design','Rectangular origami EM study maps protruding capture DNA and biotins to designed locations and measures their separations. Conformational polymorphism and flattening are characterized.','Acquire full methods and complete strands; inspect routing and12-linker-omission control separately; do not treat flattened images as authored new designs.'),
('acs.nanolett.5b02502','3756136-nl5b02502_si_001.pdf','pp2–3','design_bearing','reused_design','M13mp18 tile/frame is explicitly prepared following prior DNA transporter design, first with S2–S4 stators then walker-S1 duplex. Photocontrolled walking is observed by high-speed AFM.','Resolve reference2 and four stator/walker sequence variants; verify frame morphology separately from narrower filled-domain scope.'),
('acsnano.5b03413','3751516-nn5b03413_si_001.pdf','pp2–3','design_bearing','modified_design','DNA frames contain paired G-tract or C-tract sequences in opposite dsDNAs for G-quadruplex/i-motif formation; AFM compares separated and connected states under distinct ionic/pH conditions.','Inspect full methods, sequence image and parent frame routing; conditions are not automatically distinct strand sets.'),
('acsnano.5b06357','3739540-nn5b06357_si_001.pdf','pp2–3','uncertain','uncertain','Supplement reports four all-atom hexagonal nanotube models DNT1–4 with18/20angstrom initial helix spacing. This establishes computational structural study but inspected pages do not establish the origami scaffold/staple topology.','Inspect model-building image and main topology/parent references before deciding origami design reuse; no simulation performed here.'),
('acs.nanolett.5b04045','3734644-nl5b04045_si_001.pdf','pp1–3','design_bearing','new_design','caDNAno-designed origami pillar folds from8064nt scaffold and staple set with subsequent purification.100nm AuNP functionalization and dye-quenching controls are separately described.','Inspect TableS1, pillar routing, dye/particle anchor variants and annealing table; no complete synthesis set certified.')]

def main():
 acs={r['doi']:r for r in json.loads((L.ROOT/'acs_acquisition.json').read_text())['records']}
 for suffix,filename,loc,rel,con,note,q in SPECS:
  doi='10.1021/'+suffix;r=next(r for r in L.read('publication_reviews') if r['registry_key']==doi)
  if r['run_id']!='bootstrap-20261105':continue
  f=next(f for f in acs[doi]['files'] if (f.get('local_file') or '').endswith(filename));ev=evidence(L.ROOT/'assets'/f['local_file'],f['url'],'PDF '+loc)
  evs=[ev]
  if suffix=='acs.nanolett.5b01461':evs.append(evidence(L.ROOT/'assets/sources/pre2020-expansion/PMC4532261.xml','https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4532261/','Results Fig3 and scaffold comparison; Self-assembly and analysis Methods'))
  r.update(review_stage='design_sources_reviewed',relevance=rel,design_contributions=[con],catalog_eligibility='unresolved',evidence=evs,rationale=note,unresolved_questions=[q],access='partial',reviewer='Codex inspected named source sections',run_id='B0007',date=L.DATE)
  L.upsert('publication_reviews',r,'B0007 explicit primary-source classification; complete-set checks remain open')
 key='10.1186/1471-2105-13-138';r=next(r for r in L.read('publication_reviews') if r['registry_key']==key)
 if r['run_id']=='bootstrap-20261105':
  ev=evidence(L.ROOT/'assets/sources/PMC3496572.xml','https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3496572/','Abstract; Results TAGs for staple strands, both triangular and six-helix subsections, Figs7–8/Table9')
  r.update(review_stage='fulltext_reviewed',relevance='design_bearing',design_contributions=['modified_design'],catalog_eligibility='unresolved',evidence=[ev],rationale='EGNAS computes replacement attachment sequences for18 modified staples on Ding triangular origami and10 modified staples on Stearns6HB. It includes scaffold/staples in sequence constraints and points to Additional files7/8. These are computational design modifications; inspected sections do not report experimental validation of the redesigned sequences.',unresolved_questions=['Acquire Additional files7/8, retain parent versus redesigned sequences separately and resolve exact parent bibliographic identities.','Inspect complete article before concluding whether any experimental validation appears elsewhere.'],reviewer='Codex primary Results inspection',access='partial',run_id='B0007',date=L.DATE)
  L.upsert('publication_reviews',r,'Retain computational sequence redesign from low-keyword rotation')
 b=next(b for b in L.read('batches') if b['batch_id']=='B0007');b.update(after_counts=L.counts(),completed_actions=['Inspected all15 downloaded ACS supplements:13 design-bearing and2 unresolved topology cases.','Reviewed EGNAS primary computational attachment-sequence modifications in low-keyword rotation.'],unresolved_keys=b['input_keys'],next_queue=[k for k in b['input_keys'] if next(r for r in L.read('publication_reviews') if r['registry_key']==k)['review_stage']=='unreviewed'],validation=[L.validate()]);L.upsert('batches',b,'Checkpoint sixteen substantive B0007 source inspections; nine rotating records remain')
 print(L.validate())
if __name__=='__main__':main()
